  t("<b>6.1 The Mission</b>", "<b>Feb 1946</b> arrived (slide PYQ note: 24 March 1946); three members: <b>Lord Pethick-Lawrence</b> (SoS India), <b>Sir Stafford Cripps</b> (President, Board of Trade), <b>A.V. Alexander</b> (First Lord of Admiralty)", "Same day: <b>Naval Mutiny, Bombay</b> = British lost trust in army (board)", "<b>Only proposal offering united India + Purna Swaraj</b>", "Goal: peaceful transfer of executive power + <b>CA</b> to frame the constitution; <b>&quot;One State, Two Nation&quot;</b> solution (Syed Ahmed Khan hinted; Rajaji gestured)", w=24),
  t("<b>6.2 Proposals</b>", "<b>i) Weak centre</b>: only <b>Defence, Communications, Foreign Affairs</b>; all else + residuary with provinces = confederation (link: Rajaji 1944)", "<b>ii) No two CAs, no veto to ML1906</b>: framing by majority vote, but ML1906's overall agreement needed for the final constitution", "<b>iii) Three sections</b>: <b>A</b> = Hindu-majority provinces; <b>B</b> = NWFP, Punjab, Sindh (MMP west); <b>C</b> = Bengal + <b>Assam</b> (31% Muslim, but <b>Sylhet</b> Muslim majority)", "<b>iv) Group constitutions</b>: each section frames its own for all subjects bar D-C-FA (like Art. 370 for all 11 provinces; meets <b>14 Points March 1929</b> in spirit)", "<b>v) Union constitution</b>: only the 3 subjects; framed by CA = <b>PLA members elected Dec 1945 + nominees of Princely States</b> (as Cripps 1942)", "<b>vi)</b> CA populated by <b>Aug 1946</b>; <b>vii)</b> no change for <b>10 years</b>; <b>viii)</b> after general elections a province may leave its group; <b>ix)</b> full independence once constitution drafted", "<b>x)</b> <b>Interim govt</b> at the Centre (done <b>Sept 1946, Nehru PM</b>); <b>xi)</b> <b>advisory committee</b> on rights of citizens, tribals, minorities (not the CA); <b>xii)</b> major communal question in Central Legislature: majority of <b>both Hindu and Muslim members</b> + overall majority", w=26),
  mn("3 · 3 · 3 · 10 · 4 · 569", "Three members, three union subjects, three sections, ten years, four minimum, 569 maximum. <i>(number card)</i> Minimum = 3 group + 1 union = <b>4</b>; maximum = 565 states + 3 + 1 = <b>569</b>."),
  bx('pk', "<b>Teacher's boards:</b> Union GoI = <b>symbolic sovereignty + D, C, FA</b> + its own COI. <b>Group B (CoB)</b> = NWFP (INC), Punjab, Sindh; <b>Group A (CoA)</b> = six HMPs: UP, Bihar, Orissa, Madras, Bombay, CP; <b>Group C (CoC)</b> = Bengal + Assam (INC, 31% Muslim). 565 princely states choose to <b>sign the IOA or not</b>. <b>Pak within India = CMP 1946.</b> Mains PYQ board: <b>How Bx complicated ToP in 1940s</b>; a prince may draft his own constitution. Beside the weak-centre clause: <b>&quot;14 pt Demands&quot;</b>. CA votes by majority: the opposite of AO 1940's veto."),
  bx('pk', "<b>Permanent govt (board):</b> permanent govt comes when the Constitution is drafted and in effect; interim = temporary. Checklist: no change of constitutions for 10 years; change of group only after general elections; CA in 1946; immediate interim coalition at Centre; British said grouping compulsory."),
  bx('bl', "<b>Like today's EU (board):</b> a Union over groups, each member keeping its own head of govt; EU groupings are on language and ethnicity, A-B-C were on <b>religion</b> = 2 Nation 1 State. <b>Israel-Palestine 1948</b>: options 2N1S (union for D, C, FA with a Palestinian and a Jewish province) or 2N2S: board marks 2N2S as taken. Post-WWII partitions: <b>India, Palestine, Korea, Vietnam (1954), Europe (capitalist/communist), Germany (West/East), China-Taiwan</b>."),
