  t("<b>7.1 Debates on CMP</b>", "<b>i)</b> ML1906 wanted to question the Union constitution <b>immediately</b>, not after 10 years", "<b>ii) Grouping</b>: INC = <b>not compulsory</b> (did not want NWFP, Assam in B, C); ML1906 = <b>compulsory</b>, and the <b>British agreed</b>", "ML1906 logic: compulsory grouping = <b>implicit partition</b> (one state, two nations; Pakistan within India as Groups B and C); explicit = two states", "<b>Central fault-line</b>: INC voluntary vs ML1906 compulsory; British clarification gave Jinnah the <b>trigger</b>", "<b>iii)</b> INC wanted <b>elected</b> reps of Princely States in the CA (as in Cripps 1942)", w=24),
  t("<b>7.2 July 1946 to Dec 1946</b>", "<b>iv) July 1946</b>: INC said NWFP + Assam would not join Groups B, C; <b>Nehru</b>: only binding decision = formation of a CA", "ML1906 <b>rejected CMP</b>, refused Interim Govt and CA; <b>Direct Action Day 16 Aug 1946</b>: Calcutta riots, <b>5,000 dead in a week</b>", "<b>v)</b> ML1906 later joined the Interim Govt <b>out of fear</b> of INC alone holding power; took <b>Finance</b>, used it to make the govt unworkable", "<b>6 Dec 1946</b>: British stood for <b>two CAs</b> if ML provinces stay out", "<b>9 Dec 1946</b>: CA convened, <b>Sachchidananda Sinha</b> provisional President; <b>11 Dec 1946</b>: <b>Rajendra Prasad</b> permanent President (Prelims 2024)", "<b>Feb 1947</b>: ML1906 demanded dissolution of CA as not truly representative", w=26),
  bx('pk', "<b>Teacher's board:</b> INC said NWFP won't join B and Assam won't join C, so Jinnah gave the Direct Action call. Margin: <b>Bengal had an ML1906 govt</b>. Margin on 10-year row: <b>but initially grouping was compulsory, as per British (clarified later)</b>. CA = British India (like Rajya Sabha) + nominees of 565 PS. CA 'not truly representative' because ML had not joined. <b>Sinha = temporary, Prasad = permanent.</b>"),
  bx('ye', "<b>Source conflicts:</b> (1) CA populated by <b>Aug 1946</b> (handout, typed slide); board writes Sept 1946 'made in December 1946': use Aug 1946, CA actually met <b>9 Dec 1946</b>. (2) Mission arrived <b>Feb 1946</b> (handout) vs 24 March 1946 (slide PYQ note): use 1946 for MCQs. (3) <b>Prelims 1999 Congress leader in favour of CMP</b>: teacher's tick <b>(d) Azad</b>, Patel 'accepted but not crazy about it'; bank key says (c) Patel: <b>teacher's board wins</b>."),
  bx('gr', "<b>Slide PYQ facts (not in handout):</b> <b>Ambedkar</b> elected to CA from <b>West Bengal</b> (trap: not Bombay); CA elected by PLAs with proportional representation; Jinnah never sat in it; Constitution adopted <b>26 Nov 1949</b>, in force <b>26 Jan 1950</b>; <b>Kripalani</b> INC President <b>Dec 1946 to Dec 1947</b>. <b>Interim Cabinet 2 Sept 1946, Nehru, 12 ministers</b>: Foreign Affairs Nehru, Home Patel, <b>Finance Liaqat Ali Khan</b>, Defence Baldev Singh. Slide note: ML1906 won <b>73 of 78</b> seats in the elections under the Cabinet Plan."),
