  t("<b>Atlee Statement</b>", "In effect <b>pro-balkanisation</b>, like <b>Cripps 1942</b> (option for provinces not to join)", "British to leave by <b>30 June 1948, with or without a constitution</b> = deliberate threat of anarchy to force a compromise", "<b>6.1 Princely States</b>: all <b>565</b> not under any future GoI; <b>Paramountcy lapses</b>, not transferred: effectively 565 independent countries", "Power to <b>Interim Govt (Nehru)</b> and <b>provincial govts of provinces that had not joined the CA</b> (could become independent)", "<b>6.2 New Viceroy</b>: <b>Mountbatten (MTB)</b> to replace <b>Wavell4347</b>", "<b>Result</b>: victory for ML1906; communal violence; <b>INC-Akali-Unionist coalition in Punjab overthrown</b> by direct action led by Muslims under ML1906", w=24),
  bx('pk', "<b>Teacher's board:</b> Atlee Statement = <b>warning of anarchy</b>: no Constitution of India = no State (Legislature, Executive, Judiciary); without civil services and ministers = anarchy. Stress: <b>pro-balkanisation, 30 June 1948, British would leave, with or without a constitution</b>. Provinces outside the CA = <b>Sindh and Bengal</b>; board count <b>565 states + India + Sindh + Bengal = 568</b> possible successor states. Margin links the street-force overthrow in Punjab to Nepal and Bangladesh (check notebook)."),
  bx('ye', "<b>Numbers:</b> <b>568</b> = possible successor countries after Atlee; <b>569</b> = maximum constitutions under CMP. Different things. Slide PYQ 1999 note: Cripps's secession clause threatened up to <b>576</b> entities. Handout cites Prelims 1998 for the June 1948 deadline; no such stem on the slides."),
  sec("9 · PLAN BALKAN, APRIL 1947 " + P('2000'), 'g'),
