  t("<b>10.1 Context</b>", "MTB's brief: deadline <b>October 1947</b> to explore unity and partition options (Prelims 1998: <b>keep India united if possible</b>); in <b>2 months</b> concluded <b>CMP and unity were dead horses</b>, entirely due to Jinnah", "<b>British interest</b>: better two friendly countries than an unfriendly Pakistan; <b>Atlee: &quot;Britain wanted a united India, tried but failed.&quot;</b>", "<b>Three choices</b>: 1 India as colony; 2 friendly united India; 3 (only realistic) friendly India + friendly Pakistan", "<b>Harder point</b>: partition was avoidable if Britain had acted on communal violence, not played <b>passive mediator</b>; passivity served British interest", "<b>Dominion status</b> to both: both stay in the <b>Commonwealth</b>: trade benefits to British firms, a political win at home", w=26),
  bx('pk', "<b>Teacher's board (Cold War):</b> Pakistan was <b>geopolitically more important</b>: West Pakistan faces Central Asia, Afghanistan, Middle East, Arabian Sea; East Pakistan the Bay of Bengal; non-aligned India = plus. Pakistan joined <b>SEATO 1954, Baghdad Pact 1955</b> (US-led, NATO-like). <b>Pro-British points</b>: special dominion status (only symbolic sovereignty), two friends, Commonwealth preserved. <b>Pro-INC</b>: unofficial promise of no independence for 565 PS; India as large as possible; two strong centres, not confederations (<b>APC 1928 / Motilal Nehru Report</b> unitary); exit in <b>72 days</b>; two boundary commissions."),
  t("<b>10.2 INC's demands accepted</b>", "INC accepted partition + dominion status, so:", "<b>i)</b> <b>Small Pakistan</b>, informal promise no independence for the 565 states", "<b>ii)</b> <b>Strong unitary centre</b> (like Nehru Report 1928, unlike Rajaji 1944)", "<b>iii)</b> Exit in <b>72 days from 3 June = 15 Aug 1947</b>, a year ahead of Atlee's deadline", w=22),
  t("<b>10.3 Mechanics of partition</b>", "<b>Punjab + Bengal</b>: simple majority of <b>either</b> Hindu or Muslim PLA members for partition = partition", "<b>Sindh</b> = plebiscite; <b>NWFP + Sylhet (Assam)</b> = referendum; <b>Baluchistan</b> = vote by political leaders", "<b>Referendum, not plebiscite</b> in NWFP/Sylhet: INC won there in Dec 1945, need clear <b>binding</b> answer (plebiscite = non-binding opinion)", "Yes vote: CA splits into <b>two CAs, two dominions</b>, power to two centres on <b>15 Aug 1947 (appointed day)</b> = India an <b>'indestructible union of destructible states'</b> (power only to the Union; provinces did not decide to unite as in USA)", "INC and ML1906 <b>both accepted</b>; Punjab, Bengal voted partition; <b>NWFP, Sindh, Baluchistan, Sylhet</b> joined Pakistan", "<b>Frontier Gandhi boycotted</b> the referendum; <b>Bannu Resolution (June 1947)</b> demanded <b>Pakhtonistan</b>; NWFP went to Pakistan as his followers did not vote", "Pakistan banned <b>Khudai Khidmatgars 1948</b>; 'Pakhto' = Pakhtun code of life; some Pashtuns wanted Afghanistan; NWFP today = <b>Khyber Pakhtunwa</b>", w=28),
  t("<b>10.4 Boundary Commissions</b>", "Two (west = Punjab, east = Bengal), both headed by <b>Sir Cyril Radcliffe</b>, a British jurist who had <b>never been to India</b> (Prelims 2013: delimit India-Pakistan boundary)", "Each <b>4 judges</b>: 2 nominated by INC, 2 by ML1906: <b>deadlocked</b>, so lines = Radcliffe's unilateral decision", "<b>Radcliffe Line announced 17 Aug 1947</b>, two days after independence = maximum chaos", w=22),
  bx('pk', "<b>Teacher's board:</b> the British did not want blame for violence and migration, so the line came <b>after 15 August</b>."),
  bx('gr', "<b>Slide PYQ answers:</b> <b>United Bengal Plan (April 1947)</b> by <b>H.S. Suhrawardy</b> (ML Chief Minister of Bengal) + <b>Sarat Bose</b>: sovereign united Bengal, failed against opposition from both INC and ML1906 (Prelims 2000, answer Bengal). Handout deadline Oct 1947 = exploring options; Atlee 30 June 1948 = transfer: both stand."),
  bx('qt', "<b>Mains skeleton (board PYQ): British imperial power in complicating ToP in the 1940s.</b> Intro: British interest drove the process. Body: (1) <b>veto to ML1906</b> in AO 1940, Cripps 1942, Wavell 1945 (implicit); (2) <b>Atlee Feb 1947</b>: 565 states, non-CA provinces, balkanisation tilt; (3) <b>Plan Balkan</b>; (4) <b>passive mediator</b> on communal violence; (5) <b>dominion status</b> + Commonwealth benefit; (6) <b>Cold War</b> value of Pakistan; (7) <b>Radcliffe Line after 15 Aug</b> to avoid blame. Close: British national interest, 'tried but failed'."),
  sec("11 · INTEGRATION OF PRINCELY STATES", 'b'),
  stl(11, "Because Paramountcy lapsed without a successor, 565 states were legally free; Patel and V.P. Menon closed the gap."),
  t("<b>565 princely states</b>", "Before Aug 1947: <b>565</b> recognised states, about <b>40% of landmass</b>, <b>23% of population</b>", "<b>Indian Independence Act (July 1947)</b> ended Paramountcy over all 565: each legally free to be independent", "<b>Sardar Patel</b> (States Dept head) + <b>V.P. Menon</b> (Secretary): by persuasion, pressure, patriotism", "<b>552</b> contiguous to India; <b>549</b> signed <b>IOA</b> by or soon after 15 Aug 1947", "<b>13</b> contiguous to Pakistan acceded there: <b>Bahawalpur</b> (Punjab), <b>Khairpur</b> (Sindh), <b>Kalat, Makran, Las Bela, Kharan</b> (Balochistan), <b>Swat, Chitral, Hunza, Nagar, Amb, Phulra, Dir</b> (NW Frontier/Gilgit)", w=24),
  tb(["Holdout", "When", "How"], ["<b>K</b>ashmir (J&amp;K)", "Oct 1947", "Acceded after invasion by Pakistani-backed tribal militias"], ["<b>J</b>unagadh", "Feb 1948", "Public plebiscite, overwhelming for India; Nawab first tried Pakistan"], ["<b>H</b>yderabad", "Sept 1948", "Military operation <b>Operation Polo</b>"]),
  mn("565 = 552 + 13", "<b>552 = 549 + 3</b>: 565 total, 552 to India, 549 by accession by or soon after 15 Aug 1947, 3 later (J&amp;K, Junagadh, Hyderabad), 13 to Pakistan. <i>(number card)</i>"),
  mn("KJH", "<b>K</b>ings <b>J</b>oined <b>H</b>esitantly = Kashmir Oct 1947 &middot; Junagadh Feb 1948 &middot; Hyderabad Sept 1948. <i>Order kept: three dates in time order.</i>"),
  bx('ye', "<b>Numbers note (handout):</b> '562 states integrated' is a widely repeated error (Butler Committee 1927 cited 562). <b>565</b> is the final count; authority = <b>White Paper on Indian States 1950</b> (Ministry of States under Patel and V.P. Menon) read with the Independence Act. Teacher marks the PS slide title <b>'P11'</b> (check notebook)."),
  sec("12 · INDIAN INDEPENDENCE ACT, JULY 1947 " + P('1996'), 'r'),
  stl(11, "Because both parties accepted the Mountbatten Plan, Parliament gave it legal form."),
  t("<b>The Act = legal status to the Mountbatten Plan</b>", "<b>10.1 Partition</b> into two independent dominions on the <b>appointed day, 15 Aug 1947</b>", "<b>10.2 GG</b>: each dominion headed by a GG appointed by the <b>King</b>; same GG for both until their CAs legislate; Pakistan chose <b>Jinnah</b>", "<b>10.3 End of dominion status</b> by the CAs (India: <b>26 Jan 1950</b>)", "<b>10.4 Jurisdiction + Paramountcy</b>: Parliament's jurisdiction over British India ended; <b>Paramountcy over 565 ended, transferred to nobody</b>", "<b>10.5</b> Titles abolished: <b>Emperor of India</b>, <b>SoS for India</b> (created 1858)", "<b>10.6</b> Until a new constitution: <b>GoI Act 1935</b> applies", "<b>10.7</b> <b>Boundary commission</b> appointed by the GG", "India a <b>dominion of Britain 15 Aug 1947 to 26 Jan 1950</b>", w=26),
  mn("TABLE", "Lay it on the <b>TABLE</b> (clauses 10.3-10.7): <b>T</b>itles abolished (Emperor, SoS) &middot; <b>A</b>ct of 1935 applies &middot; <b>B</b>oundary commission by GG &middot; <b>L</b>apse of Paramountcy + Parliament's jurisdiction &middot; <b>E</b>nd of dominion status (26 Jan 1950). Headline items 10.1-10.2 (partition, shared GG) come first."),
  bx('pk', "<b>Prelims 1996 A/R (answer d, A false, R true):</b> board: <b>sovereignty = power to do L-E-J</b> (three organs). The Act ended Parliament's jurisdiction on 15 Aug 1947, so British sovereignty did not continue; but the <b>King appointed the last GG, Mountbatten</b>."),
  sec("13 · WHY PARTITION? " + P('1998'), 'g'),
  stl(10, "Because the 3rd June Plan looked sudden but was not, trace the long process behind it: four causes."),
  t("<b>Why partition</b>", "Acceptance was <b>not sudden</b>: culmination of a long process", "<b>Bipin Chandra</b>: INC failed to bring Muslims into the INM as a <b>mass constituency</b>, and failed to <b>curb Muslim communal forces</b> (esp. from <b>1937</b>)", "Proof: ML1906 won <b>90%</b> of Muslim seats in 1945 PLA elections", "By June 1947 INC gave up unity: communal violence, failed Interim Govt, ML1906 refusing the CA (Aug 1946); even Bengal's ML govt promoted riots = <b>a compulsion, not a choice</b>", w=24),
  t("<b>11.1 British Divide and Rule (DnR)</b>", "<b>i) Hunter's Indian Musalmans (1871)</b>: neglect fed the <b>Faraisi movement (1830-70s)</b>; Muslims as a separate neglected category", "<b>ii) Census 1881</b>: religion-based statistics, homogeneous religious identity", "<b>iii) 1897</b> job reservation for Muslims; <b>iv) Bengal Partition 1905</b> Muslim-majority province", "<b>v)</b> <b>Minto05-10</b> answers <b>Simla Deputation 1906</b>; <b>vi)</b> <b>ML1906</b> formed; <b>vii)</b> <b>separate electorates ICA 1909</b>", "<b>viii)</b> <b>AO 1940</b> + <b>Wavell 1945</b>: veto to ML1906", w=24),
  t("<b>11.2 WEMC Muslims</b>", "<b>Syed Ahmed Khan</b>: <b>Two-Nation Theory</b>, INC = Hindu body, reservation for the <b>Quam</b>, support to British", "<b>Four Delhi Proposals (Dec 1927)</b> + <b>three Calcutta Amendments (Dec 1928)</b> failed &rarr; Jinnah's <b>14 Points (March 1929)</b> = blueprint for ML1906 politics", "ML1906 opposed <b>CDM (1930-34)</b> + <b>QIM (1942-45)</b>", w=22),
  t("<b>11.3 Hindu Revivalism (1880s-1900s)</b>", "Arya Samaj <b>Shuddhi + cow protection</b> turned aggressive after <b>Dayanand died 1883</b>", "<b>Cow-killing riots 1893</b>; <b>Hindi-Urdu controversy</b> (1880s-1900, NWP + Awadh set up 1877): Hindi = Hindus, Urdu = Muslims", "INC <b>did not condemn 1893 riots</b> (<b>1886 rule</b> against social issues); Muslim participation fell", "<b>Swadeshi 1905-11</b>: Hindu religious symbolism, Muslims + British shown as partners in Jatras, social boycott hurt the poor; ML1906 and Ulamas discouraged", w=22),
  t("<b>11.4 Role of INC</b>", "<b>i) Cripps 1942</b>: accepted provincial autonomy for MMPs (like Art. 370)", "<b>ii) Rajaji 1944</b>: plebiscite for 'partition without independence', conceded self-determination", "<b>iii) CMP 1946</b>: opposed only <b>compulsory</b> grouping (in essence 2N1S)", "<b>iv) March 1947</b>: INC first mentioned <b>partition of Punjab + Bengal</b>", "<b>Two false beliefs</b>: <b>v)</b> partition would be <b>temporary</b> (MG: <b>&quot;don't accept partition in your hearts&quot;</b>, but hearts do not make borders); <b>vi)</b> <b>appeasement</b> would shrink the fear-of-majority complex: instead <b>LP1916, Rajaji 1944, Desai-Liaqat 1945</b> each raised ML1906's floor", w=26),
  mn("RIDE", "Four forces took India for a <b>RIDE</b> to 3rd June: <b>R</b> Hindu Revivalism &middot; <b>I</b> INC's own concessions + false beliefs &middot; <b>D</b> British Divide and Rule &middot; <b>E</b> Elite WEMC Muslims + Two-Nation Theory. <i>No fixed order in the handout, so initials rearranged.</i>"),
  bx('pk', "<b>Gandhi, alone:</b> could not start a movement against partition (communalism too wide); said Hindus and Sikhs also desired partition: Muslims hated him, Hindus and Sikhs abandoned him; by mid-1947 alone. Mountbatten: <b>'one-man boundary force'</b>. Verdict: <b>culmination of a long process, not a single failure</b>. Teacher labels this section <b>'mmp'</b> (no expansion given: check notebook)."),
  bx('gr', "<b>Slide PYQ answers:</b> winding up INC after independence = <b>Gandhi</b> (board: INC a platform of many ideologies); at independence Gandhi <b>not a member of Congress</b>, <b>Kripalani</b> President; INC accepted partition <b>to avoid large-scale communal riots</b> (c); Gandhi's alternative to partition = <b>invite Jinnah to form the govt</b>, bitterly criticised by Congress. Handout alert: Prelims 2000 for Act + integration; real 2000 stems are United Bengal, Balkan, Gandhi's alternative."),
  tb(["Who", "Role"], ["<b>C. Rajagopalachari</b>", "1944 formula author, Gandhi approved"], ["<b>M.A. Jinnah</b>", "ML1906; 2N2S; the floor-raiser"], ["<b>Bhulabhai Desai / Liaqat Ali Khan</b>", "CLA leaders; Liaqat got Finance"], ["<b>Wavell4347</b> (Viceroy 1943-47)", "Shimla 1945; declared failure"], ["<b>Atlee</b>", "PM July 1945; March 1946 anti-partition; Feb 1947 deadline"], ["<b>Pethick-Lawrence, Cripps, Alexander</b>", "Cabinet Mission: Secretary, Trade, Admiralty"], ["<b>Mountbatten</b>", "Replaced Wavell4347; Balkan; 3rd June"], ["<b>Nehru</b>", "Interim PM Sept 1946; killed Balkan"], ["<b>Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan</b>", "Frontier Gandhi; Bannu Resolution June 1947"], ["<b>Radcliffe</b>", "Both boundary commissions, never been to India"], ["<b>Patel + V.P. Menon</b>", "States Dept head + Secretary"], ["<b>Sinha / Prasad</b>", "CA provisional 9 Dec / permanent 11 Dec 1946"], ["<b>Bipin Chandra</b>", "Historian: two INC failures"]),
